  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set name = \"mne-lsl\" %}\n{% set version = \"1.14.0\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: {{ name|lower }}\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/source/{{ name[0] }}/{{ name }}/mne_lsl-{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: e2ef6a6ee9556a1f93d7e6be52e625cc27e44d06a42a711e6516e18a80d0162b\n  # HOTFIX for 1.14.0: setup.py builds liblsl with a hardcoded cmake command which\n  # ignores $CMAKE_ARGS, hence neither the conda toolchain overrides nor the\n  # -DLSL_FETCH_PUGIXML=OFF below reach that build. The missing toolchain overrides\n  # break macOS, where CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_AR (an llvm-ar which is not shipped next to\n  # the conda clang) is used to create the LTO static archive of the fetched pugixml.\n  # Fixed upstream in 1.14.1, drop the patch when updating to it.\n  patches:\n    - 0001-honor-CMAKE_ARGS-in-the-liblsl-build.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  python_version_independent: true  # [is_abi3]\n  # link liblsl against the conda-forge pugixml instead of the copy which it fetches\n  # from GitHub at build time\n  script:\n    - export CMAKE_ARGS=\"${CMAKE_ARGS} -DLSL_FETCH_PUGIXML=OFF\"  # [unix]\n    - set \"CMAKE_ARGS=%CMAKE_ARGS% -DLSL_FETCH_PUGIXML=OFF\"  # [win]\n    - {{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-build-isolation --no-deps\n  skip: true  # [py<311 or (is_abi3 and py!=311)]\n  entry_points:\n    - mne-lsl = mne_lsl._commands.main:run\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - python                                 # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cross-python_{{ target_platform }}     # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - {{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - {{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - cmake\n    - make\n  host:\n    - pip\n    - pugixml\n    - python\n    - python-abi3  # [is_abi3]\n    - setuptools >=64.0.0\n    - setuptools_scm >=7.0.0\n  run:\n    - click >=8.1\n    - mne-base >=1.6.0\n    - numpy >=1.21\n    - packaging\n    - pooch\n    - psutil\n    - pyqtgraph\n    - python\n    - qtpy\n    - scipy\n\ntest:\n  imports:\n    - mne_lsl\n  commands:\n    - pip check\n    - mne-lsl sys-info\n    - python -c \"import mne_lsl; assert mne_lsl.__version__ == '{{ version }}', mne_lsl.__version__\"\n  requires:\n    - python\n    - pip\n\nabout:\n  home: https://mne.tools/mne-lsl\n  summary: Real-time framework integrated with MNE-Python for online neuroscience research through LSL-compatible devices.\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_family: BSD\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - src/liblsl/LICENSE\n  doc_url: https://mne.tools/mne-lsl\n  dev_url: https://github.com/mne-tools/mne-lsl\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - larsoner\n    - mscheltienne\n",
